// The agents' drawer (render/drawer.h): a finger up from the strip pulls
// it open, the counts riding up as its lid and the body pressed flat
// against the top of the glass. The board tells the Mac (`ev drawer`
// "open") and the Mac's next state has the rows (`list`). Open, the body's
// eyes squeeze shut and a paw drops over the sheet's edge. A tap on a row
// sends its id (`pick`), lights it and shuts the drawer as Boop hands it
// over. Pulled open again with seven sessions, a screenful of them and
// the sixth peeking; a finger up the rows scrolls them, the board asks for
// the rows from where it has scrolled (`from`), and they come to rest on a
// whole row; it shuts itself 15 s after the last touch. Asked how many
// agents are running, Boop holds up the count, and 1.5 s on the drawer
// comes up by itself (`show`), the Mac's rows in it.
